Should be set up to minimally reproduce the error we've seen in PeleLMeX.

Compile: "make -j"

Run: "./main3d.sycl.MPI.ex"

This code just has two loops that copy data within an AMReX multifab. In both loops,
a the second component of the multifab is filled either by copying the contents of
the first component or by setting a constant value, with a boolean flag that indicates
which option will be used. In the first loop, the boolean flag is hard coded as a const,
which works. In the second loop, it can be set at runtime by the user. This causes
the code to segfault.